Tweenora

Tweenora is based on rive-runtime and rive-wasm, © Rive, MIT.

Runtime upstream: https://github.com/rive-app/rive-runtime
Base commit: daf55385b71fb861b2a1ae2930ae4492832d5db5
Upstream license and copyright: `runtime/LICENSE` (MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 Rive),
kept as they are. `runtime/renderer/LICENSE` carries the same license for the
rendering engine.

Upstream of the JavaScript and WASM layer (`web/rive-wasm/`):
https://github.com/rive-app/rive-wasm
Base commit: 589b787c8a50b528db0071d9bc22e6b21ab13604 (it pins the runtime
daf55385)
Upstream license and copyright: `web/rive-wasm/LICENSE` (MIT, Copyright (c)
2020-2021 Rive), kept as they are. The `@tweenora/webgl2` package reproduces
its text in its own `LICENSE` file.

The `@tweenora/webgl2` package also ships `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`
(`web/rive-wasm/js/npm/webgl2/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`): the full text of the licenses of the
libraries linked into `rive.wasm` (HarfBuzz, SheenBidi, miniaudio, Yoga, Luau,
libhydrogen, Emscripten, musl, libc++ and the code derived from Skia). Inventory and evidence:
`docs/baseline/licences-et-mentions.md`.

Tweenora is neither affiliated with nor endorsed by Rive. "Rive" is a trademark
of its owner; it is used here only to refer to the upstream project.

Third-party dependencies

Third-party code included in the repository keeps its own license, stated in the
header of each file:

- `runtime/tests/include/catch.hpp`: Catch2, Boost 1.0 license;
- `runtime/tests/include/args.hxx` and `runtime/skia/font_converter/include/args.hxx`:
  args (Taylor C. Richberger and Pavel Belikov), MIT license;
- `runtime/tests/include/EGL/`, `GLES3/`, `KHR/` and `runtime/renderer/glad/include/`:
  Khronos Group headers (Apache-2.0 or MIT depending on the file); the files generated by
  glad carry the notice "(WTFPL OR CC0-1.0) AND Apache-2.0".

The texts of the Apache-2.0 and CC BY 4.0 licenses, cited in this file for the
Khronos headers, Dawn, the Ultra font and the Twemoji Mozilla font, are in
`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/` (together with the text of the OFL 1.1 license).

The folders `runtime/tests/dependencies/` and `runtime/tests/unit_tests/dependencies/`
contain no file tracked by this repository: build dependencies are
downloaded into them by the build scripts, under the license they carry.
The fonts in the test folders (`runtime/tests/unit_tests/assets/fonts/`,
`runtime/tests/web_scripting/stress/text/`, etc.) keep the license of their
authors: see "Test fonts" below, then "Test files".

Code derived from Skia and Android code (BSD-3-Clause)

